/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{-2{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344550} :answer-field/id #uuid "d97c1b36-19cb-526f-a00b-7c8a56561d72" :answer-field/key "field-7" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344548} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cb133e2a-8b28-5d39-a4cd-34fa60812388" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{2{x}^{2}}(-(4xy+3x)\\,\\text{d}x+\\text{d}y)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344554} {:answer/id #uuid "9adc4c38-16d6-5ee6-be35-e292cea9bbb0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{4x}(-(4xy+3x)\\,\\text{d}x+\\text{d}y)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344555} {:answer/id #uuid "fda15913-1daf-5aab-9f9c-700d18924988" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{-4x}(-(4xy+3x)\\,\\text{d}x+\\text{d}y)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344556} {:answer/id #uuid "aa21b19a-59e6-5344-a7d8-aa63249d037a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{-2{x}^{2}}(-(4xy+3x)\\,\\text{d}x+\\text{d}y)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344557}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aa21b19a-59e6-5344-a7d8-aa63249d037a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{-2{x}^{2}}(-(4xy+3x)\\,\\text{d}x+\\text{d}y)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344557} :answer-field/id #uuid "4d1c15b7-5aec-5c81-b363-3d368e44a5f0" :answer-field/key "field-8" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344553}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b8087283-5e57-58d5-8cbc-5979c0257602" :question/math-academy-id "q-337161" :question/problem "Suppose we would like to find an integrating factor to convert the differential equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=4xy+3x\n$$\n\ninto an exact equation using an integrating factor. Select the correct options in the reasoning below.For a differential equation of the form\n\n$$\nP(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+Q(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y=0,\n$$\n\nwe have that if\n\n$$\n{{field-1}}=g(x)\n$$\n\nwhere $g(x)$ is independent of $y,$ then an integrating factor for the equation is\n\n$$\nI(x)={{field-2}}\n$$\n\nwhere $\\operatorname{exp}⁡(x)$ denotes the exponential function ${e}^{x}.$\n\nFirst, we rewrite our equation in differential form. This gives\n\n$$\n{{field-3}}.\n$$\n\nLet's denote\n\n$$\nP(x,y)=-(4xy+3x),\\,Q(x,y)=1.\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\,{{field-4}}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=\\,{{field-5}}\n$$\n\nSince for this equation \n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{Q}(\\frac{∂P}{∂y}-\\frac{∂Q}{∂x})={{field-6}},\n$$\n\nwhich depends on $x$ only, then an integrating factor for our equation is\n\n$$\nI(x)={{field-7}},\n$$\n\nand we arrive at the exact equation\n\n$$\n{{field-8}}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a differential equation of the form\n\n$$\nP(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+Q(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y=0,\n$$\n\nwe have that if\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{Q}(\\frac{∂P}{∂y}-\\frac{∂Q}{∂x})=g(x)\n$$\n\nwhere $g(x)$ is independent of $y,$ then an integrating factor for the equation is\n\n$$\nI(x)=\\operatorname{exp}⁡(\\int g(x)\\,\\text{d}x)\n$$\n\nwhere $\\operatorname{exp}⁡(x)$ denotes the exponential function ${e}^{x}.$\n\nFirst, we rewrite our equation in differential form: \n\n$$\n-(4xy+3x)\\,\\text{d}x+\\text{d}y=0\n$$\n\nLet's denote \n\n$$\nP(x,y)=-(4xy+3x),\\,Q(x,y)=1.\n$$\n\nNow, let's compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂P}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(-(4xy+3x))=-4x \\\\ \\frac{∂Q}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(1)=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{Q}(\\frac{∂P}{∂y}-\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}) & =\\frac{1}{1}(-4x-0) \\\\  & =-4x,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nis a function of $x$ only, we can conclude that an integrating factor for the equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & =\\operatorname{exp}⁡(\\int -4x\\,\\text{d}x) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{exp}⁡(-2{x}^{2}) \\\\  & ={e}^{-2{x}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand by multiplying our differential equation by the integrating factor, we have\n\n$$\nI(x)\\cdot (-(4xy+3x)\\,\\text{d}x+\\text{d}y)=I(x)\\cdot 0\n$$\n\nwhich simplifies as\n\n$$\n{e}^{-2{x}^{2}}\\cdot (-(4xy+3x)\\,\\text{d}x+\\text{d}y)=0.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186344558 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "54d19544-7156-58e9-a090-12f8e9492226" :knowledge-point/title "Testing Integrating Factors for ODEs in Differential Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "39709273-a80c-5f33-8182-4732fff32276" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{y}\\,\\text{d}x-y\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344560} {:answer/id #uuid "cd52834a-06c1-5fa5-b2ef-6ffa38872ad2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-y\\,\\text{d}x+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{y}\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344561} {:answer/id #uuid "b430f12a-fdfa-518e-be11-2b1d7fff7367" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-y\\,\\text{d}x-{x}^{2}y\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344562} {:answer/id #uuid "36314b1e-a923-58b2-81b8-0e3aa31a4090" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}y\\,\\text{d}x-y\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344563}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cd52834a-06c1-5fa5-b2ef-6ffa38872ad2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-y\\,\\text{d}x+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{y}\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344561} :answer-field/id #uuid "d8000a6d-c0f5-535a-9063-218c386a95b1" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344559} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d713bc44-c324-59f2-b0c0-797296031de4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344565} {:answer/id #uuid "e2abc863-b6a4-5c77-ab71-413802f13fd4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344566} {:answer/id #uuid "0c2e2488-7b1b-5bda-a1e7